# Heap sized for the COVERAGE-INSTRUMENTED compile, which is the worst case this build has and
# is what CI runs too. Measured 2026-07-28 by bisecting a full `clean; coverage;
# <every module>/Test/compile`:
#
#   8g  -> OutOfMemoryError in dotty.tools.dotc.transform.InstrumentCoverage
#   9g  -> passes  (the floor; 10g chosen for headroom, since the cliff is 1g wide and CI
#          runners differ from a dev Mac)
#   11g, 14g, 20g -> pass
#
# Xms is left at 5120M: the JVM starting at roughly half its ceiling avoids repeatedly growing
# the heap mid-compile, without committing the full 10g against everything else on the machine.
# This is a judgement, NOT a measurement — GC logging could not be got into the compiling JVM
# (sbt reuses a server process whose options are fixed at startup, so -Xlog via .jvmopts,
# SBT_OPTS and -J were all ignored). If you want it evidence-based, the way in is to observe a
# genuinely cold compile with -Xlog:gc and size Xms from the post-GC live set.
-Xmx10g
-Xms1g
-Xss8M
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
